# Playing guitar (issues 034, 057, 107): 32x48, drawn over the guitar's tile (col 1, row 6, against the south wall) and the tile north of it where the player stands facing down, plus the tile to the east (col 2, row 5, over the sofa's west arm). Marc plays right-handed, so the guitar is the `guitar` drawing mirrored (neck to the east, dark oak body, ink outline, sound hole) held diagonally in the lap, with a hand on the neck. Placed at x 0, y -16 from the guitar piece (poses.ts); it replaces both the player and the `guitar` sprite (replacesPiece), so the bottom rows draw the EMPTY floor stand (drawn from Marc's real wooden folding stand seen from above: two flat bars in a V with black rubber dots, joined at a padded block at the west end; no brand): the guitar has been lifted off it. The rows below the tile are empty.
size: 32x48
